{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"artifacthub/community-operators/prometheus","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:16:57.215Z","source":{"name":"Artifact Hub","api":"https://artifacthub.io/api/v1/packages/olm/community-operators/prometheus","page":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/olm/community-operators/prometheus"},"readme":"The Prometheus Operator for Kubernetes provides easy monitoring definitions for Kubernetes services and deployment and management of Prometheus instances.\n\nOnce installed, the Prometheus Operator provides the following features:\n\n* **Create/Destroy**: Easily launch a Prometheus instance for your Kubernetes namespace, a specific application or team easily using the Operator.\n* **Simple Configuration**: Configure the fundamentals of Prometheus like versions, persistence, retention policies, and replicas from a native Kubernetes resource.\n* **Target Services via Labels**: Automatically generate monitoring target configurations based on familiar Kubernetes label queries; no need to learn a Prometheus specific configuration language.\n\n### Other Supported Features\n\n**High availability**\n\nMultiple instances are run across failure zones and data is replicated. This keeps your monitoring available during an outage, when you need it most.\n\n**Updates via automated operations**\n\nNew Prometheus versions are deployed using a rolling update with no downtime, making it easy to stay up to date.\n\n**Handles the dynamic nature of containers**\n\nAlerting rules are attached to groups of containers instead of individual instances, which is ideal for the highly dynamic nature of container deployment.","readmeBase":"https://github.com/k8s-operatorhub/community-operators/operators","publisher":{"name":"Operator Framework","url":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/search?org=operator-framework","official":false,"verified":false,"cncf":false},"registered":null,"updated":"2024-04-01T16:45:00.000Z","categories":["Monitoring and logging"],"keywords":["prometheus","monitoring","tsdb","alerting","observability","Monitoring"],"license":null,"links":[{"name":"Prometheus","url":"https://www.prometheus.io/"},{"name":"Documentation","url":"https://github.com/prometheus-operator/prometheus-operator/tree/master/Documentation"},{"name":"Prometheus Operator","url":"https://github.com/prometheus-operator/prometheus-operator"},{"name":"source","url":"https://github.com/prometheus-operator/prometheus-operator"},{"name":"Community Operators repository","url":"https://github.com/k8s-operatorhub/community-operators/operators"}],"maintainers":[{"name":"Red Hat","email":"openshift-operators@redhat.com"}],"stats":{"pulls":null,"stars":36,"subscriptions":11},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"0.70.0","digest":"sha256:8816163883247868042","pushed":"2024-04-01T16:45:00.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.65.1","digest":null,"pushed":"2023-05-05T18:09:45.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.47.0","digest":null,"pushed":"2021-04-15T23:43:00.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.32.0","digest":null,"pushed":"2019-09-04T12:00:00.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.37.0","digest":null,"pushed":"2019-09-04T12:00:00.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.15.0","digest":null,"pushed":"2019-01-08T16:12:00.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.27.0","digest":null,"pushed":"2019-01-08T16:12:00.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.22.2","digest":null,"pushed":"2019-01-08T16:12:00.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null},{"name":"0.14.0","digest":null,"pushed":"2019-01-08T16:12:00.000Z","size